    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4593A\n\nSPONSOR: OBERACKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nfor imposition of additional sales tax in the county of Schoharie\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Schoharie County Board of Supervisors to impose an\nadditional one percent sales tax for a two year period.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 1210 of the tax law to extend the authori-\nzation for Schoharie County to impose an additional one percent (1%)\nsales tax until November 30, 2025.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe law expires on November 30, 2023.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation needs to be renewed in 2023 so that the county can\ncontinue to collect the additional tax without interruption. Requested\nby the Schoharie County Board of Supervisors (Res. No. 28).\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThe law was previously extended by Chapter 61of the laws of 2017 in an\nomnibus measure (A.40001).\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate\n",
